<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="7f1f232c">&lt;p&gt;
    Controls should be:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Accurate&lt;/strong&gt; – generate data and information for effective managerial decision making&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Timely&lt;/strong&gt; – decision makers have immediate access to measures to respond meaningfully&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Flexible&lt;/strong&gt; – can be updated quickly or modified as changes occur, such as unanticipated threats or
    opportunities&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Acceptable&lt;/strong&gt; – easily understandable by all people affected&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Integrated&lt;/strong&gt; – consistent with corporate values and culture and enforceable through organizational
    policies.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Feasible&lt;/strong&gt; – economically balanced cost against benefit and reasonable to operate&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Strategic&lt;/strong&gt; – placed and emphasized where failures cannot be tolerated, often where time loss and money
    cost risk failures are greatest&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Correctible&lt;/strong&gt; – identified deviations can be fixed and in some instances, suggestions for correction are
    provided within&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Work on the Exception Principle&lt;/strong&gt; – only important deviations are called out, attention is on errors or
    non-conformity, not on conformity itself, allowing managers to eliminate unnecessary supervision&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="90a7063f"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="a31814a">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of this work product is to make certain that an organization complies with established rules and
    applicable laws and regulations, meets business requirements, and also to protect organizational financial and
    management data and other assets.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Controls set performance standards, offer a means to measure performance and trigger corrective action when necessary.
    In financial reporting, effective controls reduce the risk of asset loss and help validate that information is complete
    and accurate, financial statements are reliable and comply with laws and regulations. Internal controls, in accounting
    and auditing, are measures for assuring achievement of organization’s objectives in operational effectiveness and
    efficiency, reliable financial reporting, and compliance with laws, regulations and policies. Technical controls are
    mechanisms used to regulate operations to meet policy requirements.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="3a4365e6"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="8c330434"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="42f2f0b5">&lt;p&gt;
    The attributes of this work product include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control ID
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control objective
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control definition
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control type (preventive, detective, corrective)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control nature (manual, IT dependent manual, automated)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control frequency
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Applicability to client
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Justification for inclusion
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Whether the control is implemented or not
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Justification for exclusion
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    In a multi-site, large and complex organization, it is recommended to include three additional attributes in the
    Controls List that provide details per control regarding &quot;Control Designed by&quot;, &quot;Control Implemented by&quot; and &quot;Control
    Operated by&quot;. These three additional attributes provide information regarding the interfaces and dependencies for
    each control within scope of the management system.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
